+
+  test('A->B->A finding: the re-send is cross-entry, so a per-entry Set would not address it', () => {
+    // Measured live (List -> Map -> List -> Map): the map material key is
+    // reported twice, so an A->B->A cycle DOES re-send. But every List/Map
+    // toggle creates a new history entry with a distinct entryId
+    // (99918f5e… -> 7e8347e8… -> d810b731… -> 5dcd41f5…), so the two map
+    // reports live under DIFFERENT entryIds. A Map<entryId, Set<key>> would
+    // change nothing: the second lookup misses on the entry key itself, not
